{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["Zerach — on account of the second one, who is the red one. And 'zerach' means reddishness, as written: והצרעת זרחה במצחו. And likewise every rising of the sun, in the morning and in the evening, is red, as written: ויהי בבקר והשמש זרחה על המים ויראו מואב מנגד את המים אדומים כדם. And so in Bava Batra, in 'the one who sells the ship': this sun is a red one, and this one that is not red but pale and blotchy — because its light is not strong — on account of the illumination of the great day."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The Aramaic passage from Bava Batra (83a) is rendered literally; the rabbinic text has variant readings and the phrase בפניא ורמשא (pale and blotchy) is translated without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:43.529670059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}